      "created_at": "2014-07-28T20:14:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Train puns, that's the ticket!</p><p>It does seem like it's our default mode of communication, and any thread will end up there eventually.&nbsp;</p><p>It reminds me of the ecological process of succession, where bare rock is colonised by organisms which make the conditions suitable for the next species which make things liveable for the next ones, and so on until you get a stable mature ecosystem (for example in my area that would ultimately be oak woodland).</p><p>We go from a retracted question to train puns fairly quickly.&nbsp;</p>",
